## Why This Is Asked
This interview question explores cross-region, multi-tenant data routing with dynamic policy-driven enrichment, end-to-end observability, and integration of AWS data primitives beyond basic pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region routing with tenant isolation
- OPA-driven enrichment at ingestion with hot policy refresh via changelog stream
- Idempotent writes to S3 Parquet and DynamoDB
- AWS Glue catalog integration with Athena for analytics
- OpenTelemetry end-to-end tracing
- Per-tenant DLQ handling and retry strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: ingestion Lambda
async function processRecord(record, ctx) {
  const tenantId = extractTenantId(record);
  const region = extractRegion(record);
  const enriched = await enrichWithOPARules(record, tenantId);
  await writeToS3Parquet(enriched, tenantId, region);
  await writeToDynamoDB(enriched, tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end streaming ingestion, lightweight validation, data quality scoring, and practical cost governance in a beginner-friendly setup.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams + Lambda ingestion
- Lightweight JSON validation and 0–100 data quality scoring
- Parquet storage in S3 with region/date partitioning
- DLQ handling for invalid records
- DynamoDB for regional budgets and a guard lambda to pause ingestion
- Lifecycle policies for cost control; CloudWatch observability

## Code Example
```javascript
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const r of event.Records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(r.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString('utf8'));
    const ok = validate(payload);
    if (!ok) {
      await sendToDLQ(payload);
      continue;
    }
    const score = computeQuality(payload);
    await writeParquetToS3(payload, score);
  }
  return { status: 'ok' };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution and optional fields in this pipeline?
- How would you validate and recover from late data while respecting the budget guard?
- What monitoring dashboards would you build to track data quality, cost, and DLQ trends?

## Why This Is Asked
Privacy and compliance demand masking at ingestion, not post-hoc. The candidate should design an isolation boundary for unmasked data, ensure per-tenant access controls, and plan end-to-end lifecycle.

## Key Concepts
- Ingestion-time PII masking with tenant isolation
- Per-tenant KMS keys and IAM-based access controls
- Dual data stores: masked data in a shared lake and unmasked in a restricted vault
- Glue catalog and Athena for querying masked data; DynamoDB for audit trails
- Data lifecycle and testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record, tenantKey) {
  // pseudo-implementation
  record.phone = redact(record.phone);
  record.name = redact(record.name);
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking correctness at scale?
- What are the latency and cost trade-offs of this approach?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, observable streaming pipeline with data masking in AWS DVA.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming patterns with Kinesis and Lambda
- Data redaction for PII in JSON payloads
- Parquet files in S3 with date/hour partitioning
- Error routing to DLQ and event auditing in DynamoDB
- X-Ray tracing and LocalStack test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(payload){
  if(!payload) return payload;
  if(payload.email) payload.email = payload.email.replace(/[^@]+@[^.]+\.[^.]+/g, 'REDACTED');
  if(payload.phone) payload.phone = payload.phone.replace(/\d/g, 'X');
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate redaction accuracy at scale?
- How would schema changes impact the validator and redactor?

